   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">By 31 December 2021:   
1. 4 private sector Business Development Service (BDS) providers delivered on-line training, advisory and mentoring to approximately 100 beneficiaries from the creative sector.
2. COVID Safe Business Protocol signages for MSMEs were launched by the Minister for Commerce, Trade, Tourism and Transport (MCTTT) in August 2021, and 3,000 COVID Safe signage packs for MSMEs were distributed by partners MCTTT, Fiji Commerce and Employers Federation, Suva Retailers Association (SRA), Fiji Competition and Consumer Commission (FCCC) and Ministry of Employment to assist MSMEs comply with new COVID legislation and avoid fines and imprisonment. 
(a) A Child Labour poster was also included in the package as a collaboration between the MPTF project and MAP16 project. 
(b) 24 business advisory products for MSMEs were developed and videos finalised to help MSMEs alert their customers about COVID-19. By 31 December 2021: 
1. ILO provided technical advice for the development of joint training programmes on technical (creative/agriculture) and business. 
2. Provided training on ILO&apos;s Activity-Based Learning (ABL) methodology and materials on Community Based Enterprise Development (C-BED) to 4 private sector BDS providers. 
3. Developed COVID-19 Safe Business Protocols advisory notes in written, audio-visual and mobile app.  The materials include steps for formalisation of MSMEs. Printing of signages for hard hit MSME compliance.</narrative>
